WEBVTT

00:03.006 --> 00:05.010
[Ishikawa] <i>The</i> Damocles' <i>descent
is increasing in speed!</i>

00:05.427 --> 00:06.764
[Yoko] <i>If we don't do something,</i>

00:06.847 --> 00:09.393
<i>the units deployed in Ebetsu City
will be caught in the destruction.</i>

00:09.561 --> 00:12.483
I'll try controlling
the remaining float via the backdoor.

00:12.609 --> 00:14.278
-[beeping]
-I'm in!

00:15.280 --> 00:17.451
Its energy is draining rapidly.

00:17.869 --> 00:19.330
<i>There's no avoiding a crash.</i>

00:19.540 --> 00:21.084
[Kuroto] Can you buy us some time?

00:21.585 --> 00:24.340
[Rozé] If I can adjust
the energy flow, maybe...

00:24.423 --> 00:26.261
-Give it a shot.
-[Rozé] <i>Roger!</i>

00:26.762 --> 00:30.394
I need you to control it so it falls
somewhere there would be few casualties.

00:30.477 --> 00:31.479
Can you do it?

00:31.772 --> 00:32.899
[Rozé] I'll do my best.

00:32.983 --> 00:35.195
Ms. Araki, please share the data.

00:38.536 --> 00:39.538
[grunts]

00:40.707 --> 00:42.334
I'll provide cover for their evacuation.

00:42.418 --> 00:43.588
Got it.

00:44.380 --> 00:46.802
Haruka squad, switch to Ortygia support.

00:46.885 --> 00:47.887
[Haruka] <i>Roger that.</i>

00:47.971 --> 00:48.973
[Rozé] <i>General Kuroto.</i>

00:49.056 --> 00:51.645
<i>How about Okahoro Park
for the landing point?</i>

00:51.729 --> 00:52.897
That should work.

00:53.398 --> 00:55.695
Monobe squad, Iwamoto squad,
proceed to 3 o'clock.

00:55.778 --> 00:58.199
Oda squad, Munemori squad, to 8 o'clock.

00:58.283 --> 00:59.285
[soldiers] <i>Roger that!</i>

00:59.703 --> 01:01.080
[Rozé] <i>We're running out of time.</i>

01:01.832 --> 01:03.001
Hurry, everyone!

01:08.428 --> 01:11.184
[Yoko] <i>All units have been evacuated
to a safe distance!</i>

01:11.267 --> 01:13.021
[Ishikawa] <i>The float is
no longer responding.</i>

01:13.104 --> 01:14.357
<i>The</i> Damocles <i>is falling!</i>

01:14.649 --> 01:17.822
[Yoko] <i>It will make landfall
before reaching the landing point.</i>

01:34.230 --> 01:35.357
[sighs in relief]

01:37.111 --> 01:38.363
[Kuroto] <i>Well done.</i>

01:39.323 --> 01:40.367
<i>You have my thanks.</i>

01:44.041 --> 01:46.045
[♪ opening theme song playing]

03:15.390 --> 03:16.977
IMPERIAL PALACE
LORD NORLAND'S MANSION

03:17.060 --> 03:18.981
[reporter on tv]
<i>As announced by the government,</i>

03:19.064 --> 03:22.195
<i>the mission to annihilate Sapporo
using the</i> Damocles <i>was--</i>

03:23.991 --> 03:26.120
The <i>Damocles</i> and young Divock...

03:26.872 --> 03:29.794
The results don't quite
justify the sacrifice...

03:30.337 --> 03:31.798
[Norland] No, they are sufficient.

03:32.341 --> 03:33.719
You may go now.

03:33.802 --> 03:34.804
Excuse me.

03:39.104 --> 03:41.985
So... what's next?

03:42.069 --> 03:44.114
You have something in mind, don't you?

03:45.325 --> 03:47.371
Can we put that thing of yours to use?

03:47.705 --> 03:51.630
We did manage to catch
several soldiers in the Sapporo Ghetto

03:51.713 --> 03:53.466
trying to help the Elevens escape.

03:54.426 --> 03:56.765
<i>They're showing symptoms
like what we saw in Abashiri,</i>

03:56.848 --> 03:59.144
<i>claiming to have no memory
of what occurred.</i>

04:00.438 --> 04:02.610
Guess we'll have
to interrogate them thoroughly.

04:05.448 --> 04:06.952
SEVEN SHINING STARS HAKODATE HIDEOUT

04:07.035 --> 04:10.291
Whew! Can't believe we made it back alive!

04:10.626 --> 04:11.795
Hear, hear.

04:11.878 --> 04:14.634
We didn't exactly come out unscathed.

04:15.135 --> 04:18.391
[Oda] But we could've
easily been wiped out.

04:18.474 --> 04:19.519
It's a miracle.

04:20.019 --> 04:22.482
Guess we have the Nameless Mercenary
brothers to thank.

04:23.151 --> 04:24.153
Agreed.

04:24.654 --> 04:27.827
They shot down the debris, for one,
and controlled the float.

04:28.119 --> 04:29.956
[Oda] Speaking of which,
where are those two?

04:30.457 --> 04:33.421
[Shota] They went with General Kuroto
to see Dr. Einstein off.

04:33.505 --> 04:35.133
Then they're taking a few days off.

04:35.216 --> 04:37.597
What's up with that? No fair!

04:37.680 --> 04:40.435
Call it the perks of being
contract mercenaries.

04:40.519 --> 04:42.648
[Oda] While we
have to keep slaving away...

04:42.732 --> 04:44.443
You're hardly "slaving away."

04:44.527 --> 04:46.447
<i>-Get to work already.</i>
-[Oda] <i>I'm working my butt off!</i>

04:46.531 --> 04:47.950
BLACK KNIGHTS MATSUMAE LOGISTICS FACILITY

04:48.994 --> 04:50.497
[Nina] Thank you for everything.

04:50.581 --> 04:51.666
[Kuroto] Likewise.

04:52.167 --> 04:55.716
Our lives were saved
by the F.L.E.I.J.A. Eliminator.

04:55.800 --> 04:57.177
You have our gratitude.

04:57.595 --> 04:59.348
I should be thanking you.

04:59.431 --> 05:00.935
Thanks to all of your efforts,

05:01.435 --> 05:04.441
we were able to rid the world
of the F.L.E.I.J.A.

05:08.157 --> 05:10.203
Thank you as well, Ms. Sakai.

05:10.286 --> 05:12.750
Hardly, it was an honor to accompany you.

05:14.128 --> 05:17.927
I will remain here and serve as a liaison
to the Black Knights.

05:19.388 --> 05:20.516
[Kuroto] Well then...

05:26.945 --> 05:29.491
I pray that all your wishes come true.

05:29.576 --> 05:32.540
I'll help in any way I can.

05:32.623 --> 05:34.627
[Rozé] Right. Thank you.

05:40.764 --> 05:42.225
NEO-BRITANNIA GOVERNMENT OFFICE
FRONT SHRINE

05:42.309 --> 05:43.645
[Catherine] So...

05:43.729 --> 05:46.233
it seems the mission failed.

05:46.902 --> 05:49.072
Di was real ambitious.

05:49.156 --> 05:51.578
Maybe it was his vanity
that got him killed.

05:52.287 --> 05:53.289
Is that so...

05:53.999 --> 05:58.216
That concludes my report. Bye then.

06:00.596 --> 06:01.598
[Sakura] Wait...

06:03.351 --> 06:05.355
Were there any military casualties?

06:06.065 --> 06:10.198
Well, considering all the combat,
there were bound to be some casualties.

06:10.991 --> 06:11.993
[Sakura] I see...

06:13.037 --> 06:15.375
My condolences
to those who lost their lives.

06:16.418 --> 06:17.420
And also,

06:17.505 --> 06:21.513
may I ask you to provide aid
for the injured Japanese people?

06:21.846 --> 06:23.349
Don't start with that.

06:23.432 --> 06:25.604
You're just a puppet empress.

06:25.688 --> 06:27.107
Don't overstep your boundaries.

06:27.650 --> 06:29.904
All you're doing
is creating more work for me.

06:30.698 --> 06:32.409
[Sakura] So what you're saying

06:32.910 --> 06:35.164
is that you're not incapable
of doing it, correct?

06:37.168 --> 06:40.174
I may not possess any power,

06:40.718 --> 06:42.638
but I want to do what I can.

06:42.722 --> 06:46.395
Look, just leave that kind of thinking
to people who are actually strong--

06:46.478 --> 06:48.065
I want to become strong!

06:52.992 --> 06:56.206
You've got some nerve!
You're just a puppet!

06:58.587 --> 07:00.173
[Catherine] Walther!

07:00.256 --> 07:03.304
Guard the empress for me!
From now until tomorrow!

07:03.387 --> 07:04.389
[Walther] Huh?

07:04.473 --> 07:08.690
[Catherine] I'm stronger than you,
so you better listen to me! Got it?

07:09.692 --> 07:11.028
Understood.

07:13.909 --> 07:16.455
Today is the anniversary
of Governor Jugo's death.

07:18.877 --> 07:22.008
Are you certain
you do not wish to visit his grave?

07:23.052 --> 07:26.684
Many lives were lost
in the battle we just had.

07:26.810 --> 07:31.318
Visiting my parent's grave
at a time like this would be selfish.

07:32.070 --> 07:33.489
My apologies.

07:35.786 --> 07:37.163
He was well-loved, wasn't he?

07:38.249 --> 07:40.461
Governor Jugo was a benevolent man.

07:41.673 --> 07:44.720
[Kuroto] <i>He treated Japanese
and Britannians equally,</i>

07:44.804 --> 07:47.977
<i>always making those around him smile.</i>

07:48.645 --> 07:50.398
<i>Princess Sherry was the same.</i>

07:50.481 --> 07:53.070
<i>The two were well-suited for each other.</i>

07:53.655 --> 07:54.657
<i>However...</i>

07:55.199 --> 07:57.580
<i>Princess Sherry fell ill at a young age,</i>

07:57.663 --> 08:00.919
<i>and Governor Jugo,
under the pretense of an execution,</i>

08:01.003 --> 08:03.884
is said to have been killed
by Neo-Britannian soldiers...

08:07.098 --> 08:11.566
I... killed... Jugo Sumeragi.

08:16.366 --> 08:17.661
[Sakuya] <i>He...</i>

08:18.538 --> 08:19.874
<i>killed my father...</i>

08:21.836 --> 08:23.339
[car door opens, closes]

08:26.679 --> 08:28.600
Once this battle is over,

08:28.683 --> 08:31.940
I want to move their graves
to the same location.

08:32.608 --> 08:33.860
Will you help me?

08:34.277 --> 08:36.240
Yes, of course...

08:38.327 --> 08:39.329
Thank you.

08:40.456 --> 08:41.626
BLACK KNIGHTS HACHINOHE BASE

08:41.709 --> 08:45.383
[Kaoru] It seems that Dr. Einstein
has safely arrived at headquarters.

08:46.009 --> 08:47.011
I see.

08:47.930 --> 08:50.351
[Kaoru] Second-Lieutenant Sakai
doesn't know Princess Sakuya...

08:50.434 --> 08:52.438
that is, Rozé's identity yet, does she?

08:53.440 --> 08:55.278
No, I haven't told her.

08:56.405 --> 08:58.535
She's an earnest and honest individual.

08:59.035 --> 09:03.586
She won't be able to carry out her duties
while keeping that secret.

09:05.256 --> 09:10.266
The United Federation of Nations
plans to send another peace delegation

09:10.349 --> 09:13.982
now that Neo-Britannia has lost
the <i>Damocles</i> and the F.L.E.I.J.A.

09:14.900 --> 09:18.115
[Shiro] We'll just need to be prepared
to respond immediately,

09:18.198 --> 09:22.040
no matter how the situation unfolds.

09:22.833 --> 09:26.633
We must maintain
even closer contact with Hokkaido.

09:26.716 --> 09:28.553
[Shiro] <i>That's what we need Sakai for.</i>

09:30.682 --> 09:32.352
[Mei] Thank you for stopping by!

09:34.481 --> 09:36.026
[groans]

09:45.419 --> 09:48.718
[Mei] Oh, the check? One moment, please.

09:48.802 --> 09:50.096
[woman] Thank you for the meal!

09:50.179 --> 09:51.724
Please come again!

09:51.808 --> 09:53.978
[Vallen] Mei, sandwich for Table 1.

09:54.062 --> 09:55.064
Got it!

09:58.822 --> 10:00.282
Business seems to be booming.

10:00.366 --> 10:01.536
[Mei] Good morning!

10:05.459 --> 10:08.550
[man 1] Mei, can I get a glass of water?
And a wet towel as well.

10:08.633 --> 10:09.635
Sure thing!

10:09.718 --> 10:11.597
[man 2] Oh, could I get the check?

10:11.681 --> 10:12.975
[Mei] Right, coming up.

10:13.058 --> 10:15.354
[Vallen] Mei, it's okay.
I'll take care of it.

10:15.438 --> 10:17.275
[Mei] Sorry, boss.

10:17.818 --> 10:19.404
Please come again.

10:20.741 --> 10:22.870
Hey, you know... I could help.

10:22.953 --> 10:25.667
Don't worry about it. This is my job.

10:26.293 --> 10:28.213
It's not like I'm here all the time.

10:28.297 --> 10:30.092
I could at least help with the shopping.

10:30.635 --> 10:32.054
Really?

10:33.892 --> 10:35.896
Why this outfit?

10:36.229 --> 10:38.484
It really does suit you.

10:40.906 --> 10:41.908
[Sakuya] <i>Wait!</i>

10:42.283 --> 10:43.285
<i>Ash?</i>

10:44.287 --> 10:45.624
<i>Seriously?</i>

10:45.707 --> 10:48.045
<i>Talk about bad timing!</i>

10:48.128 --> 10:50.090
<i>For now, let's just get through this...</i>

10:50.174 --> 10:51.343
[Ash] What a coincidence!

10:52.596 --> 10:54.390
Are you out shopping too, Raspberry?

10:54.474 --> 10:56.938
[Sakuya] No! I mean... yes...

11:00.779 --> 11:04.452
So... Ash, are you really
headed the same way as me?

11:04.912 --> 11:08.545
I just don't want what happened to Mei
to happen to you. Don't worry about me.

11:08.628 --> 11:11.049
[Sakuya] <i>Easier said than done.
My emotions are all over the place,</i>

11:11.132 --> 11:13.805
<i>but this guy really doesn't hold back
in expressing how he feels.</i>

11:15.099 --> 11:17.938
[Ash] By the way,
I haven't seen you at the cafe lately.

11:18.021 --> 11:19.482
Have you been feeling unwell?

11:20.150 --> 11:23.741
I'm the same as always.
My health is my only redeeming quality.

11:23.825 --> 11:25.119
I know!

11:25.202 --> 11:27.123
Next time,
I'll bring you something nutritious.

11:27.206 --> 11:28.877
Are there any foods you don't like?

11:28.960 --> 11:31.006
Anything you can't eat or are allergic to?

11:31.089 --> 11:33.343
You know, our Butcher
only eats tuna-flavored kibble...

11:33.427 --> 11:34.889
[Sakuya] <i>How did this even happen?</i>

11:34.972 --> 11:36.517
[Ash] Also, recently, I...

11:38.897 --> 11:39.898
[Sakuya] Ash?

11:41.819 --> 11:42.946
<i>Is that...</i>

11:43.573 --> 11:45.367
<i>Narah Vaughn of the Einberg...?</i>

11:46.369 --> 11:49.000
Sorry, I just remembered something urgent.

11:49.083 --> 11:50.169
If you'll excuse me.

11:50.670 --> 11:52.674
Please look after yourself, Raspberry.

11:52.758 --> 11:53.760
[Sakuya] Wait...

11:55.179 --> 11:56.181
Here.

11:56.641 --> 11:59.145
A small token of appreciation
for always visiting Sumari.

11:59.647 --> 12:00.899
Thank you.

12:02.026 --> 12:03.529
[Sakuya] Please come by again.

12:03.946 --> 12:06.451
[Ash] Very well. I swear I will.

12:08.038 --> 12:09.165
Until next time.

12:10.334 --> 12:12.004
I have somewhere I need to be.

12:12.506 --> 12:13.800
You go ahead.

12:13.883 --> 12:15.219
[soldiers] Yes, my lord.

12:30.917 --> 12:32.294
[Narah] So it was you.

12:33.296 --> 12:36.846
It's been a while
since we last talked, Ash.

12:37.889 --> 12:38.891
It has.

12:40.144 --> 12:42.899
Not since I left Norland.

12:43.568 --> 12:45.070
That would make it around two years.

12:45.697 --> 12:48.201
[Narah] <i>Feels like
it was just the other day.</i>

12:50.540 --> 12:53.378
[Sakuya] <i>These two... are in contact?</i>

13:09.494 --> 13:11.540
Sir Walther Lindstedt...

13:12.166 --> 13:14.797
I'm here today as acting bodyguard
for Her Majesty the Empress.

13:15.882 --> 13:17.051
[Walther] Please, this way.

13:20.098 --> 13:21.644
It's been a while.

13:21.727 --> 13:23.355
Has it been two years already?

13:23.981 --> 13:26.069
You seem in excellent health as always...

13:31.121 --> 13:33.960
The Lindstedt and Luxembourg families

13:34.043 --> 13:39.011
moved here as Princess Sherry's aides
when she got married.

13:40.890 --> 13:43.729
[Walther] You protect the Japanese
in the special district.

13:44.105 --> 13:47.737
I kill Japanese
as a Neo-Britannian soldier.

13:48.573 --> 13:51.494
Our paths diverged. That's all.

13:53.708 --> 13:55.712
-[knocks on door]
-[gasps]

13:58.425 --> 13:59.468
Empress Sakuya.

13:59.553 --> 14:00.555
Natalia!

14:01.139 --> 14:02.726
It's been a while.

14:02.809 --> 14:05.607
Yes, it really has... I've missed you.

14:06.775 --> 14:08.863
Tell me everything.

14:08.946 --> 14:09.948
Of course.

14:13.163 --> 14:15.375
I'm glad to see you're well.

14:15.877 --> 14:17.881
[Sakura] And you, Natalia,
haven't changed a bit...

14:18.423 --> 14:22.724
By the way, there's this cat
who's been frequenting the café lately.

14:22.807 --> 14:23.809
A cat?

14:25.437 --> 14:29.236
Yes, a very lazy and troublesome cat.

14:29.988 --> 14:32.744
Although she's a beauty
and seems to have been well-raised.

14:33.244 --> 14:34.915
I'd love to meet her sometime.

14:35.457 --> 14:36.459
By all means...

14:37.587 --> 14:40.425
[Sakura] By the way, I heard about
the Special Administrative District

14:40.551 --> 14:43.264
you've implemented in your domain.

14:43.599 --> 14:47.022
Thank you for protecting the Japanese.

14:47.106 --> 14:49.569
[Natalia] Oh... It's nothing.

14:49.987 --> 14:53.326
[Sakura] I hope to implement a similar
system throughout the nation someday,

14:53.911 --> 14:56.249
though I lack the power right now.

14:56.875 --> 14:59.506
But I'll do what I can.

15:00.340 --> 15:02.971
I believe that every little bit of effort
to create change

15:03.681 --> 15:08.440
can help fulfill someone's wishes
or bring them happiness.

15:08.941 --> 15:12.866
How admirable.
I hope you can fulfill your aspirations.

15:13.491 --> 15:14.493
Thank you.

15:17.917 --> 15:22.635
Ash, if you were alive,
why didn't you contact me?

15:23.804 --> 15:25.725
Why become a terrorist...?

15:26.225 --> 15:27.269
And you?

15:27.352 --> 15:29.273
Why work under Norland?

15:29.733 --> 15:31.779
You know my reasons.

15:36.245 --> 15:38.083
I'm not asking you
to return to the military.

15:38.793 --> 15:41.464
But please. Stop opposing us.

15:42.341 --> 15:45.180
[Narah] <i>I can use my power
to help you escape abroad.</i>

15:45.765 --> 15:47.602
<i>Or defect to the Britannia Republic--</i>

15:47.685 --> 15:49.313
-[Ash] <i>Never!</i>
-[static]

15:49.480 --> 15:50.525
[Sakuya] <i>Out of range?</i>

15:54.991 --> 15:56.202
[biker] Hey! Hold on, girlie!

15:56.285 --> 15:57.580
Hand over the keys!

16:01.087 --> 16:02.590
Here, take 'em...

16:08.184 --> 16:10.857
[Narah] <i>Still can't forgive Norland?</i>

16:11.567 --> 16:13.111
<i>Or yourself?</i>

16:13.696 --> 16:14.698
[Ash] <i>Both.</i>

16:15.950 --> 16:17.579
[Narah] I told you before.

16:18.329 --> 16:21.377
Jugo Sumeragi's death wasn't your fault.

16:22.171 --> 16:24.258
Don't twist the facts.

16:26.220 --> 16:28.893
You didn't kill Jugo Sumeragi.

16:29.853 --> 16:31.147
He didn't?

16:31.480 --> 16:33.944
[Narah] If you're attempting to atone
for your sins, it's pointless.

16:34.028 --> 16:36.324
[Ash] It's not like that. I made a vow.

16:36.658 --> 16:37.660
[Narah] A vow...?

16:42.795 --> 16:44.381
And what about you?

16:44.465 --> 16:47.597
There must be another way
without having to work for Norland.

16:47.972 --> 16:48.974
For that...

16:49.433 --> 16:51.437
I determined this
was the best course of action.

16:52.899 --> 16:54.485
You've witnessed it yourself.

16:55.070 --> 16:57.115
After the fall of the Britannian Empire,

16:57.199 --> 17:00.497
behind the seemingly peaceful
facade of the world.

17:00.915 --> 17:03.086
<i>The intense hatred against Britannians...</i>

17:05.048 --> 17:09.265
Violence, theft,
discrimination, lynching...

17:11.853 --> 17:15.360
[Narah] <i>And even Lavender Home
had its victims.</i>

17:16.780 --> 17:20.120
The children from the orphanage
where you and I grew up.

17:22.542 --> 17:24.504
That's why I made a vow.

17:24.587 --> 17:26.758
Even if it means being used by Norland,

17:27.217 --> 17:29.346
I will do all I can
as a Neo-Britannian soldier

17:29.848 --> 17:32.770
to create a safe haven for those children.

17:34.273 --> 17:36.360
Even if it means fighting me?

17:36.778 --> 17:38.114
[Narah] <i>What choice do I have?</i>

17:38.406 --> 17:41.037
[Ash] <i>That man
will never keep his promise!</i>

17:41.120 --> 17:44.794
<i>Have you forgotten what he made me do?
Me, his adopted son?!</i>

17:45.253 --> 17:49.303
[Narah] I know what your life
with Norland was like.

17:50.430 --> 17:51.683
[Ash] Even so?

17:53.687 --> 17:55.023
Even so.

18:00.492 --> 18:02.245
It seems we're at an impasse.

18:03.707 --> 18:05.418
[Ash] I understand your decision.

18:10.513 --> 18:12.809
[Sakuya] <i>He didn't kill my father?</i>

18:13.476 --> 18:16.525
<i>And he's Norland's adopted son?</i>

18:17.442 --> 18:19.572
<i>How can that be?</i>

18:26.628 --> 18:28.464
[cats mewing]

18:31.053 --> 18:32.180
Give me a minute.

18:32.765 --> 18:34.686
You'll get your food after this.

18:34.769 --> 18:37.399
[Ash] Come on. I said after this.

18:39.571 --> 18:40.573
Dinner's ready.

18:40.990 --> 18:42.702
Can you clear the table?

18:42.785 --> 18:44.664
[Rozé] Yeah, sure.

18:46.000 --> 18:47.002
[Ash] Here.

18:48.755 --> 18:49.883
Thanks for cooking.

18:55.268 --> 18:57.230
[Rozé] Hey, Ash...

18:57.648 --> 18:58.650
Hm?

19:00.028 --> 19:01.030
What is it?

19:01.113 --> 19:02.115
[Rozé] Oh, nothing.

19:02.617 --> 19:04.662
Just wondering what you were up to today.

19:06.040 --> 19:07.292
The usual.

19:07.710 --> 19:10.048
Trained, looked after the weapons,

19:10.131 --> 19:11.593
then went into town for a bit.

19:12.219 --> 19:13.221
You?

19:14.891 --> 19:17.062
Me too... the usual.

19:17.730 --> 19:20.318
Met with collaborators,
gathered information...

19:20.903 --> 19:21.905
[Ash] I see...

19:22.405 --> 19:23.407
Yup...

19:25.538 --> 19:27.875
[Ash] <i>Have you forgotten
what he made me do?</i>

19:27.959 --> 19:29.253
<i>Me, his adopted son?!</i>

19:30.673 --> 19:33.386
[Narah] <i>You didn't kill Jugo Sumeragi.</i>

19:38.062 --> 19:39.732
[man groaning, screaming in pain]

19:39.816 --> 19:41.193
It wasn't me!

19:41.695 --> 19:43.532
I remember now.

19:43.615 --> 19:45.995
Someone ordered me to do it...

19:47.665 --> 19:49.586
It was... No!

19:50.044 --> 19:51.506
I can't remember...

19:51.590 --> 19:54.344
Please believe me, Sir Christoph!

19:56.181 --> 19:57.475
[Scissorman] Interesting.

19:58.562 --> 20:04.364
Looks like it was worth digging up
that destroyed Geass-related data...

20:06.243 --> 20:07.245
Do it.

20:07.329 --> 20:08.749
[whirring]

20:17.642 --> 20:18.644
[squelching]

20:18.727 --> 20:21.148
[screaming]

20:22.526 --> 20:23.737
Tell me.

20:23.820 --> 20:25.741
Who gave you the orders?

20:28.079 --> 20:31.293
They had... blond hair...

20:34.174 --> 20:35.511
[Scissorman] <i>Is he dead?</i>

20:37.222 --> 20:39.978
Looks like it still needs adjustments.

20:40.562 --> 20:42.065
[Scissorman] <i>But it worked.</i>

20:42.440 --> 20:44.570
<i>And we still have plenty of test subjects.</i>

20:45.113 --> 20:47.535
<i>Can't wait to see what comes out next.</i>

20:47.618 --> 20:49.162
Give me more.

20:50.289 --> 20:51.458
More.

20:58.055 --> 21:02.480
[Natalia] <i>By the way, there's this cat
who's been frequenting the café lately.</i>

21:02.690 --> 21:03.692
[Sakura] <i>A cat?</i>

21:04.026 --> 21:05.027
[Natalia] <i>Yes,</i>

21:05.111 --> 21:08.075
<i>a very lazy and troublesome cat.</i>

21:08.325 --> 21:11.415
<i>Although she's a beauty
and seems to have been well-raised.</i>

21:11.498 --> 21:12.710
[chuckles softly]

21:16.801 --> 21:18.972
-[Walther] Puppet empress.
-[gasps]

21:22.145 --> 21:23.815
Sakuya Sumeragi.

21:25.527 --> 21:27.238
[gasps, grunts]

21:28.575 --> 21:32.499
Yet even that is a lie.

21:34.545 --> 21:35.798
Isn't that right,

21:36.716 --> 21:38.678
Sakura Haruyanaginomiya?

21:40.473 --> 21:42.477
[♪ closing theme music playing]

24:05.387 --> 24:07.391
Translated by Kenji Mouri
